pper.INDEX_MAPPER_SOURCE_MODE_SETTING` it fails back to synthetic in the case of logsdb."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/logsdb/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/logsdb/SyntheticSourceIndexSettingsProvider.java","id":34936,"created_at":"2024-11-01T14:58:25Z","original_position":12,"side":"RIGHT","position":14,"submitted_on_commit":"e16e68cbd8562f36674a020c3bfe6827291a2827","diff_hunk":"@@ -101,6 +101,18 @@ boolean newIndexHasSyntheticSourceUsage(\n \n         try {\n             var tmpIndexMetadata \u003d buildIndexMetadataForMapperService(indexName, templateIndexMode, indexTemplateAndCreateRequestSettings);\n+            var indexMode \u003d tmpIndexMetadata.getIndexMode();\n+            if (SourceFieldMapper.INDEX_MAPPER_SOURCE_MODE_SETTING.exists(tmpIndexMetadata.getSettings())\n+                || indexMode \u003d\u003d IndexMode.LOGSDB\n+                || indexMode \u003d\u003d IndexMode.TIME_SERIES) {\n+                // in case when index mode is either tsdb or logsdb and only _source.mode attribute is specified, then the default could\n+                // be wrong. However, it doesn\u0027t really matter, because if it is set to stored, then adding index.mapping.source.mode has\n+                // no effect. And _source.mode can\u0027t be set to disabled, because that isn\u0027t allowed with logsdb/tsdb.\n+                var sourceMode \u003d SourceFieldMapper.INDEX_MAPPER_SOURCE_MODE_SETTING.get(tmpIndexMetadata.getSettings());\n+                return sourceMode \u003d\u003d SourceFieldMapper.Mode.SYNTHETIC;","submitted_line":112},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"- The added logic to check for `SourceFieldMapper.INDEX_MAPPER_SOURCE_MODE_SETTING.exists(tmpIndexMetadata.getSettings())`, `indexMode \u003d\u003d IndexMode.LOGSDB`, and `indexMode \u003d\u003d IndexMode.TIME_SERIES` is clear and necessary.\n- The comment explaining the conditions under which `_source.mode` can be set to `SYNTHETIC` is helpful but could be expanded to clarify why these speci